# This directory *is* the disposable $HOME (see .envrc), so a session writes
# its own state here. Name what a session is known to write, and nothing
# more: anything unnamed lands in `git status` as an untracked file, which is
# how this room finds out that something new pollutes it.
#
# Adding a line is therefore a discovery, not housekeeping -- say what wrote
# it. Clearing the room is `git clean -xd home/`, and the -x is needed
# precisely because these paths are ignored.
#
# A trailing `#` is not a comment here: it becomes part of the pattern, and
# the pattern then matches nothing. Comments go on their own line.

# Re-include everything first: the user's ~/.config/git/ignore hides
# `**/.claude/settings.local.json`, `**/CLAUDE.local.md`, `tmp/`, and `*.log`
# in every repo, and each of those is something this room needs to see. What
# the room reports must not depend on a file outside the repo.
!/**

# Claude Code's config dir, per .envrc. These six appear under `claude -p`.
/.config/claude/.claude.json
/.config/claude/.credentials.json
/.config/claude/.last-cleanup
/.config/claude/backups/
/.config/claude/projects/
/.config/claude/sessions/

# The rest were added by the room's first interactive session, 2026-08-10.
# None of them appear under `claude -p`; see
# ../background.kb/interactive-startup-populates-the-room.md

# the changelog, and a lookup of the account's closed issues
/.config/claude/cache/

# every prompt typed in the room, verbatim
/.config/claude/history.jsonl

# the official plugin marketplace, cloned on first interactive start
/.config/claude/plugins/

# the copy of the binary it installs for itself, and its staging area
/.cache/claude/
/.local/share/claude/
/.local/state/claude/

# registered during the login flow
/.local/share/applications/claude-code-url-handler.desktop

# Claude Code shells out to `gh`, which finds no config of its own here
/.cache/gh/
/.local/state/gh/
